#' A synthetic myDAR walk
#'
#' A 6-second LiDAR walk past a wall and a parked car on a road, generated by
#' the myDAR test suite from a scene with known geometry, run
#' through the myDAR processing pipeline and read with
#' \code{\link{read_mydar_walk}(max_points = 6000)}. Coordinates are meters
#' from the walk origin. Use it to try the \code{mydar_*_view()} functions
#' without the packages the readers need.
#'
#' The raw walk files it was read from ship in
#' \code{system.file("extdata", "mydar-synthetic", package = "myIO")}.
#'
#' @format A \code{mydar_walk}; see \code{\link{read_mydar_walk}} for its
#'   elements.
#' @source myDAR CLI output for the synthetic test walk;
#'   \code{tools/build-mydar-synthetic-walk.R} in the myIO repository rebuilds
#'   it.
"mydar_synthetic_walk"
